<%# GRAPH -- the studio's own records as ONE shape (#96, facelift 4/4).
    One page, one force-directed SVG: every project, job, candidate and proof
    the signed-in owner can see, joined by the containment and pick lines
    between them. Read-only, and the page is a NAVIGATION surface: clicking a
    node focuses it and its neighbourhood, and `open record` goes to the record
    it was drawn from.

    The page carries NO data of its own -- the engine fetches `/graph.json`
    (the same route, the JSON shape) and draws it. The markup here is the
    controls and the stage; the nodes are built in app/javascript/graph.js.

    The layout is a three-track grid: the controls rail, the stage, and the
    details panel. It collapses to one column under 1100px, where the panel
    moves BELOW the stage rather than squeezing the SVG into a strip. %>
<div class="page-head">
  <div class="page-head-row page-head-row--split page-head-row--stacked">
    <h1 class="section-title"><span class="gradient-text">Graph</span> — the studio, as one shape</h1>
    <%# The machine-readable twin, on the SAME route: `/graph` is the page and
        `/graph.json` is the document, the way `/audit` and `/audit.json` are one
        route. The JSON is what an agent reads; the page is what the operator
        looks at, and both come off one route so neither can drift from the other. %>
    <%= link_to "JSON", graph_path(format: :json), class: "btn btn-secondary head-action head-action--top",
                title: "The same graph as JSON — the shape an agent reads",
                aria: { label: "Graph as JSON" } %>
    <p class="page-head-blurb">Every project, job, candidate and proof this studio holds <strong>a file for</strong>, drawn as one shape: which projects are active, which candidates came from which runs, which proofs hang off which picks, and where the errored runs cluster. A record whose artwork is gone is left out — that is data debt, not work, and <a href="<%= audit_path %>">audit</a> is where it is counted. A node's colour is its <strong>kind</strong> (project, job, candidate, proof); the ring around it is its <strong>state</strong> (running, error, pass, fail) — a state is never the same colour as a kind. Read-only, and every node opens the record it came from.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="graph-layout" data-graph-root>
  <%# The controls rail. One control per question the graph can be asked: find a
      node by name, show or hide a KIND, limit the neighbourhood to N hops, and
      decide how many labels are legible. %>
  <div class="gpanel card">
    <div class="card-head">
      <h3>Graph</h3>
      <span class="tech-tag mono" id="gcount">loading…</span>
    </div>

    <label class="field" for="gfind">find
      <input id="gfind" type="search" placeholder="record name" list="gnode-list" autocomplete="off">
    </label>
    <datalist id="gnode-list"></datalist>

    <fieldset class="field gtypes">
      <legend>kind</legend>
      <%# One checkbox per ENTITY CLASS (GraphData::TYPES). The kb's page has one
          per TIER, which is the same idea: the filter is on what a node IS, and
          the state ring is drawn separately so the two never compete. %>
      <div class="check-row">
        <% %w[project job candidate proof].each do |type| %>
          <label class="check">
            <input type="checkbox" data-gtype="<%= type %>" checked>
            <span class="gdot gdot--<%= type %>"></span><%= type %>
          </label>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <label class="field" for="ghops">hops
        <select id="ghops">
          <option value="0">all</option>
          <option value="1">1</option>
          <option value="2">2</option>
          <option value="3">3</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="field" for="glabels">labels
        <select id="glabels">
          <option value="auto">auto</option>
          <option value="all">all</option>
          <option value="none">none</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>

    <div class="actions-row">
      <button type="button" id="grelax" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">relax</button>
      <button type="button" id="gfit" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">fit</button>
    </div>

    <p class="ghelp">drag a node to pin it · double-click to unpin · scroll to zoom · tab to a node and Enter opens its record</p>
  </div>

  <div class="gstage">
    <svg id="gsvg" role="img"
         aria-label="The studio's projects, jobs, candidates and proofs as a force-directed graph. Use the find field, the kind filters, or tab to a node and press Enter to open its record.">
      <g id="gedges"></g>
      <g id="gnodes"></g>
    </svg>
    <noscript><p class="jev-note">The graph needs JavaScript. The records it draws are on the project pages.</p></noscript>
  </div>

  <%# The details panel: what the focused node IS, and the way through to the
      REAL record. Empty until a node is selected -- it is the answer to "what
      did I just click", not a second graph. %>
  <aside class="gdetails card" id="gdetails" aria-live="polite">
    <div class="card-head">
      <h3>Record</h3>
      <span class="tech-tag">read-only</span>
    </div>
    <div id="gdetails-body" class="gdetails-body"></div>
  </aside>
</div>
